!
! How many neighbours of a memory map overlap (mockingbird_rules.h MR2),
! in Trebago. The regions come one to a row, sorted by base, each base ..
! base + size - 1; the pair i, i + 1 overlaps (or is out of order) when
! base(i) + size(i) > base(i + 1), which min(1, max(0, ...)) counts for
! integers. 0 is a clean map. Every base and size is 0 .. 2^48 and every
! region ends inside 2^48 (a 48-bit address space): bad counts the rows
! that do not, and the count is divided by 1 - min(1, their sum), a
! division by zero, refused, never answered. overlaps.kron answers any
! integers: past the address space the two disagree and it is held.
trebago region_overlaps
  in  base(n), size(n)
  out count
  var bad(n)
  bad(i) = min(1, max(0, 0 - base(i))) + min(1, max(0, 0 - size(i))) &
         + min(1, max(0, base(i) + size(i) - 281474976710656))
  count = sum(i = 1:n-1, min(1, max(0, base(i) + size(i) - base(i+1)))) &
        / (1 - min(1, sum(i, bad(i))))
end
